- SQLite (https://sqlite.org), in the public domain, through rusqlite's
  bundled build (MIT).
- Other crates under permissive licenses (MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD-2-Clause,
  BSD-3-Clause, BSL-1.0, Zlib, Unicode-3.0, CC0-1.0, 0BSD, Unlicense) or
  MPL-2.0 (used unmodified; its source is on crates.io). deny.toml lists
  the licenses allowed. To list every crate in the Windows build with its
  license:

      cargo deny --locked list --layout crate

